+# v28 — reduce repeated map recognition
+
+v27's narrower safe surface makes Acme Nexus (#46), for example, require a
+short pan from Seal Stone (#45). That target otherwise lands in the protected
+right-hand strip. The short pan remains necessary; this update reduces the
+recognition work it triggers.
+
+Map opening no longer adds a full fixed pause after expensive recognition: processing time counts toward the observation interval, while observations remain at least 0.15 seconds apart. Held cursor movement is faster, and progress checks can cover up to 240 reference pixels. The stationary 0.18-second endpoint hold before release remains. The extra 8-pixel target padding is removed as requested; input uses the marked boundary itself.
+
+The last measured screenshot during a held drag now counts as the first map
+alignment observation after the stationary endpoint pause. A fresh post-release
+screenshot confirms it. If the map moved, recognition runs again and another
+stable observation is required. A timestamp guard requires at least 0.15 seconds
+between observations. Flat/unrecognisable frames still need actual recognition;
+recovery and periodic absolute atlas refreshes are retained. Fresh pre-click
+movement checks, loading waits, inspection and gem confirmation are retained.
+
+The v27 safe input outline is unchanged. Map dragging and location selection
+exclude the upper-left Loong Haven title, legend, entire right-hand strip,
+shown character portrait bubble including its glow, zoom slider and bottom
+Back/region controls. Regression checks explicitly cover the title and bubble.
+
+The v24/v26/v27/v28 full-route comparison includes timing and matching/capture counts for each
+route point. It requires the no additional held movements or map distance compared with v27 while
+reducing repeated recognition and captures. These are simulated atlas results,
+not measured live BlueStacks pass times.
+
+Close the old app, extract the full folder and launch its LoongLens.exe. Saved
+routes, settings, history and screenshots remain in %LOCALAPPDATA%\LoongLens.
+The 7z includes the EXE, source, assets, models, tools, tests and validation.
+
+The timing model includes actual processing time and virtual input/loading waits in one clock, so recognition can satisfy the map observation interval. The same Windows runner measures all four versions sequentially. The resulting full-pass and per-view model times remain offline simulations, not live game measurements.
